.DS_Store

# Content sources. Only the SRD folder is tracked: everything else under data/ is either
# generated (card art, extracted from a PDF nobody may redistribute) or content the DPCGL
# re-use grant doesn't cover — playtest material and homebrew.
#
# `data/*` and not `data/*/`: a source folder may be a SYMLINK into a private content repo, and
# git treats a symlink as a file, so the trailing slash would let it through and `git add -A`
# would commit it. Matching everything and re-including what's tracked covers both, and names no
# unpublished content in a public repo.
data/*
!data/srd/
!data/sources.json
data/srd/card-art/

# Working notes, and the books they're taken from. Both are symlinks into that same private
# repo. Ignored here rather than in .git/info/exclude so the rule travels with a fresh clone.
TODO.md
CLAUDE.md
*.pdf
